    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Shake It Off",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "defensive",
      "traits": [
        "fortune",
        "primal"
      ],
      "text": "Frequency once per day\n\nTrigger Narseigus fails or critically fails a saving throw against a condition or adverse effect (such as Cursed Metamorphosis)\n\n---\n\nEffect Narseigus rerolls the triggering saving throw and uses the better result.",
      "frequency": {
        "max": 1,
        "per": "day"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Quickened Casting",
      "actions": "free",
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "concentrate",
        "spellshape"
      ],
      "text": "If Narseigus' next action is to cast an occult spontaneous cantrip or an occult spontaneous spell of 4th level or lower, he reduces the number of actions to cast it by 1 (minimum 1 action)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Steady Spellcasting",
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "If a reaction would disrupt Narseigus' spellcasting action, he attempts a DC 15 Flat check. On a success, the action isn't disrupted."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Worm Form",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "morph",
        "occult"
      ],
      "text": "Narseigus partially transforms his lower body into that of a cave worm. He can use only his tail unarmed Strike and his burrow and climb Speeds while in this form. This transformation lasts for 1 minute."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Worm's Feast",
      "actions": 2,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "primal"
      ],
      "text": "Frequency once per day\n\n---\n\nEffect Narseigus calls forth a brood of infantile cave worms to feast on his enemy's flesh. One creature within 30 feet must attempt a DC 27 Fortitude save save.\n\n---\n\nCritical Success The worms writhe away harmlessly.\n\nSuccess The target takes 2d6 piercing damage and 4d6 persistent piercing damage.\n\nFailure The target takes 6d6 piercing damage and 4d6 persistent piercing damage.\n\nCritical Failure As failure, plus the target is Off-Guard as long as it takes persistent piercing damage.\n\n---\n\nNote: A DC for this ability was not provided by Paizo. The DC present here is a moderate DC for the creature's level based on the Gamemastery Guide creature building rules",
      "frequency": {
        "max": 1,
        "per": "day"
      }
    }
